{
  "name": "alpha_crowd_lowtier",
  "description": "Legacy-alpha stage 0, low tier: the same measurement as alpha_crowd.json with the 'Low' list of featuretable.txt for the settings that matter in a crowd (avatar limits and LOD, far clip, water, particles, shadows, reflections, SSAO, texture size), to be run in a 1920x1080 window. Sorted alpha is the only transparency path of a GPU without OpenGL 4, so method 0 is the number that matters here; on such a GPU method 1 falls back to sorted. RenderMaxTextureResolution only affects textures fetched afterwards: set it before login or relog. A full-avatar crowd (all avatars drawn, RenderAvatarMaxNonImpostors raised) is the worst case for alpha; this tier limits it to 3.",
